From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:18:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: duo.config: support a per-app firewall

Enable what an application firewall such as OpenSnitch needs: NFQUEUE (nftables and xtables) to hold a
new connection while the user decides, the proc connector and kprobes for its process monitor, UDP socket
diag to match UDP flows to processes, and nft log.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/duo.config | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config b/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
index f053df9e1..5156b55db 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
@@ -483,3 +483,14 @@ CONFIG_VIDEO_DW9719=m
 # CONFIG_ARCH_VISCONTI is not set
 # CONFIG_ARCH_XGENE is not set
 # CONFIG_ARCH_ZYNQMP is not set
+# Per-app firewall (OpenSnitch): NFQUEUE to hold a new connection until the user answers, the proc connector and
+# kprobes for its process monitor, UDP socket diag for matching UDP flows, nft log for its audit rules
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_NETLINK_QUEUE=y
+CONFIG_NFT_QUEUE=y
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_NFQUEUE=y
+CONFIG_NFT_LOG=y
+CONFIG_CONNECTOR=y
+CONFIG_PROC_EVENTS=y
+CONFIG_KPROBES=y
+CONFIG_KPROBE_EVENTS=y
+CONFIG_INET_UDP_DIAG=y
